  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The logarithm reverses the action of the exponent. The principle is:\n\n$$\n{log}_{b}⁡({b}^{x})=x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $b=10$ and $x=4.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n{log}_{10}⁡({10}^{4})=4.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
